            <ArticleTitle>A potent and selective indole N-type calcium channel (Ca(v)2.2) blocker for the treatment of pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>869-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2010.11.067</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>N-type calcium channels (Ca(v)2.2) have been shown to play a critical role in pain. A series of low molecular weight 2-aryl indoles were identified as potent Ca(v)2.2 blockers with good in vitro and in vivo potency.</AbstractText>
